          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            By
            %em adiabatic quantum computation
            one means models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+quantum+systems"} parameterized quantum systems
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gates"} quantum gates
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+transformations"} unitary transformations
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} gapped
            (and possibly
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topologically ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+state"} ground state
            which are induced, via the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} quantum adiabatic theorem
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type+theory"} parameters
          %p
            Often the term
            %em adiabatic quantum computation
            is used by default for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/optimization+theory"} optimization
            problems (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+annealing"}> quantum annealing
            ”, see the references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#QuantumAnnealingReferences"} below
          %p
            On the other hand, the possibly most prominent example of adiabatic quantum computation is often not advertized as such (but see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#CLBFN15"} CLBFN 2015
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+computation"} topological quantum computation
            by adiabatic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braiding
            of
            %a{:href => "braid+group+statistics#AsBraidingOfDefects"} defect anyons
            (whose positions is the external parameter, varying in a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#FreedmanKitaevLarsenWang03"} Freedman, Kitaev, Larsen &amp; Wang 2003, pp. 7
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#NayakSimonSternFreedman08"} Nayak, Simon, Stern &amp; Freedman 2008, §II.A.2 (p. 6)
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#ChengGalitskiDasSarma11"} Cheng, Galitski &amp; Das Sarma 2011, p. 1
            %a{:href => "#ArovasSchriefferWilczekZee85"} Arovas, Schrieffer, Wilczek &amp; Zee 1985, p. 1
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Stanescu20"} Stanescu 2020, p. 321
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BarlasProdan20"} Barlas &amp; Prodan 2020
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/AnyonBraidingSchematics.jpg", :width => "640px"}/
